Z||000005||Nashco||12-09-2001||04:56 PM||||I know your car has high miles, so there are a lot of little things going on...but you've done a ton of work to the main guts of the car.  Why do you want to start over, I don't get it?  I love working on my car to improve it, but the fruits of the labor are even better than the labor <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you decide you don't want the 88 coupe, I'd like a little info.  I'm looking to build a race car out of an 88 coupe, so a "nice" car will probably be out of our spending range.  We could part it out, but I'd hate to do that with a car that is in good shape otherwise.<P>If you are wanting to sell a bunch of the stuff you mentioned above, as if you were parting that stuff out (???), I am sure you wouldn't have a problem selling it.  The engine/tranny/seats in particular are all good items.<P>Oh, you've got email too.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
